For your amusement my 2nd best game ever....

So once again a Chaotic Orc Wizard seeks the Amulet of Yendor (about
2/3 the chars i play are this combo).  This is time his name is
Garfield.  He's got a ring of +2 gain Constitution and a ring of See
Invisible. It starts out badly tho.  His faithful kitten is killed on
the first level by a falling rock trap.  Undaunted he delves deeper
into the dungeon.  On level two still shocked that he has survived this
long he finds the entrance to the mythical Gnomish Mines.

At this point he's only a low level Conjurer.  Should he go in the
mines or continue down the main dungeon?  Having heard for months about
how innocent orcs are slaughtered in the mines, he decides to come back
for the mines later.  Besides he heard that on a level called Sokoban
there might be a Bag of Holding or a Amulet of Reflection.  Both sound
like useful items.

Down he goes further.  A couple tins of spinach and pusing a few
boulders around, make him really strong (18/04).  He befrinds another
kitten which quickly turns into a housecat.  He tries to save a dog
from a pit, but was viciously attacked.  A quick prayer to Anhur saves
him from what would have been certain death and then he force bolts the
dog into oblivion.  He also happens to kill a floating eye which was
behind the door which was behind the pit.  What strange mental acuity
he has after eating the floating eye.  He finds an egg and what seems
to be a magic whisle.  He also befriends two more kittens .

On level 5 he finds Delphi.  The Oracle wants too much money so he
decides to smash all of their statues.  Wow three spellbooks were in
the statues, Magic Missle, Knock, and Levitation.  Only problem is that
even with all that strength he still needs to put something down.  Oh
well no need to carry around the books, when he's got everything in
memory (right?).

The next level he finds a 2nd staircase up and checks it out.  His cats
and kittens are left below (figuring he'll be able to retame them if
necessary).

Ugh.  So that's why it's named Sokoban.  It's just like playing that
awful awful game.  Who on earth could think this is fun?!?  Luckily he
had read the related spoiler before entering the dungeon and knew the
solutions. :-)

Yikes how did a chickatrice get in his pack?!?  Why is it calling him
Daddy?!?  Hey where did that egg go?  Ah-ha! I get it.  Oh well a pet
cockatrice could be useful.

After four agonizing levels of Sokoban (and many many uses of the
whistle to get that stupid 'trice from behind the boulders), he reaches
the zoo.  Frankly at this point a Bag of Holding would have been
prefered over the Amulet of Reflection.  However the RNG knew this and
therefore gave him the "oR.  Still it's a useful item.  In addition to
the "oR, he leaves with a large number of wands, scrolls, rings and
more food than he can carry (litterally!).  He had to leave a stash on
the frist level of Sokoban.

Now he returns to the main dungeon. Cats and kittens are still tame,
but WTF?!? the cockatrice is attacking them.  NOOOOO!  It turned one of
them to stone.  ARGH!  It turned another one to stone.  BAD BAD 'trice.
 Stop that!  I said stop that!  Alright you asked for it.  Force Bolt
to oblivion.  Hmmm what's that thunder?  @#$#$!@ I was too late, all of
the cats are stone.

Ok now what? He's only a Thaumaturge, can he handle the mines yet? He
wanders back up, but he does putz around on each level long enough to
become a Magician before he reaches the mines.

Only worry so far is that he still only has a quarterstaff for a
weapon.  However he's become very skilled with it and on the first
level of the mines, kills everthing with one hit.  A couple more levels
just like the first and he's suddenly in Mine Town.  Oh what luck, a
co-aligned temple.  Sac 'em corpses.  A booming voice "Use my gift
wisely" and what's this on the alter?  Magicbane!  Oh yeah we rock!  A
couple more corpses to sac so we can pray and make some holy water.

Now use the alter to check and see if he has any cursed items.  Why no
not a one.  In fact his mattock is even blessed.  Therefore he can wear
this 2nd ring of Gain Constituion.  That should be more useful than a
ring of See Invisible.  Ohhh it's a +3 ring, Con is 18 now!  (What does
Con do again??) Alright back to finding things to sac.  Oh a white
unicorn and he's in the temple even.  Let me killl him and sac him.
Oh he didn't leave a corpse.  How annoying.

Hey did that unicorn kill the Priest?  where did that priest go?  Ooops
excuse me sorry about that I didn't see you there.    The dumb priest
is invisible.  OUCH!  Oh let me chat and make nice with him.  "Thou
wouldst have words, eh?  I'll give thee a word or two!"  OUCH!

"Would you like your possessions identified?"

#$@#@#$!@#

Alright is there someway to calm down the priest?  This is actually the
2nd time I've had one get angry at me.  I guess a scroll of taming
would work.  Would anything else?

Random thoughts ...

Wizards should not be played like a Valkyrie.  I've gotten a lot better
but as the one near death experience proves, I've still got to be more
careful with Wizards.

this is the first time I've decided to skip the mines (on the rare
ocassion I survive long enough to make it to the entrance of the
mines).  I read a bunch of posts in this group about Sokoban vs. Mines
and was swayed in favor of Sokoban at least for Wizards and low HP
chars.  The whole BoH vs. "oR debate at my level is just theoraticl.  I
needed a BoH very badly at the time.  I'm sure later the amulet would
have save my life, but it didn't help with the angry priest (not that
the bag would either, but I could have carried more stuff).

weapons for wizards.  I generally stick with the quarterstaff until I
get Magicbane.  I do pick up daggers and darts and throw them around to
save Pw.  In my longer games, I normally run across a runed broadsword
close to my end.  Sometimes I use it, but it generally seems to take a
lot more hits to take out a gnome.  I've used a unicorn horn as a
weapon before and that seemed to work about as good as the
quarterstaff.  Other weapons seem to work a lot more poorly.  The most
useful weapon still is the Wizard's Force Bolt (and Magic Missle if I
find a spell book for it).  Of course I would expect that as what's the
point of being a wizard if you're not going to blast them from afar?
Is there anything I'm missing here?

ID items.  I really need to take more time and figure out what I've
found.  I had a /oDeath! which would have dealt with the priest.  i'm
sure Anhur wouldn't have been pleased, but I think I'd be alive.  Of
coruse  figuring that one out that wand would be difficult anyway
